  bootwright / cluster rsh
      Open an SSH session on a cluster node's Machine. By default, log in with the Machine's
      SSH identity. For a different account, supply --ssh-user <user> and --ssh-id-file
      <private-key>. That account must already accept the corresponding public key. An unproved
      host key requires interactive confirmation before SSH offers a credential. The exit
      status is the client's. The session opens on the Machine behind one node of an
      OpenShiftCluster or managed CephCluster: --node selects the node by name, then by FQDN,
      and defaults to the administrator node that cluster info names. For an OpenShiftCluster,
      the default is its first node in name order, and --node also accepts <role>-<ordinal>
      with a zero-based ordinal in that order (for example, controlPlane-0 or worker-0).
      External CephClusters are inapplicable.

  Usage
    bootwright cluster rsh [flags]

  Command flags
      --name  Select the exact object name (required)
      --node  Select a declared node by name, then FQDN (default: the cluster's administrator
              node)

  Common flags
      --ascii       Use ASCII status markers
      --color       Select terminal colors (values: auto, always, never) · default auto
      --context     Select a context (default: current context)
      --detail      Select human detail (values: compact, full) · default compact
      -h, --help    Show help for this command
      -o, --output  Select output mode (values: text, json, yaml) · default text
      --progress    Select progress animation (values: auto, always, never) · default auto
      --width       Set presentation width (0: automatic) · default 0

  More detail
    Use --help --detail full to include SSH overrides.

  Examples
    bootwright cluster rsh --context lab --name storage --node node-1
